    "title": "Carbamazepine-DTG interaction lowers DTG levels",
    "message": "Guidelines state carbamazepine decreases DTG concentrations by 30-70% and recommend using valproic acid instead. Carbamazepine was started 2 weeks ago, and the viral load rose from <50 to 1,240 copies/mL despite reported good adherence. This interaction is a likely contributor to virologic failure. The patient is already on sodium valproate, making carbamazepine potentially redundant. No alternative cause for the viral load rise is documented.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Replace carbamazepine with valproic acid or another non-interacting antiepileptic. If carbamazepine cannot be stopped, consider DTG 50 mg twice daily and repeat viral load in 2-3 months.",
