    "title": "Carbamazepine toxicity with hyponatraemia",
    "message": "Carbamazepine level is 14 mcg/mL (therapeutic 4-12), with symptoms of ataxia, nystagmus, and tremor. Sodium is 128 mmol/L, consistent with carbamazepine-induced SIADH. ALT is mildly elevated at 68 U/L, which may also reflect carbamazepine hepatotoxicity. The plan to reduce the dose is appropriate, but close monitoring of sodium and liver enzymes is needed given the compounding risk of toxicity and hyponatraemia.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
